<task id="022" project="spaarkeai-compose-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>Rebased operation log per dirty session (FR-03) — ProseMirror Mapping</title>
    <phase>2 Frontend capture</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Extends the capture core (`.ts`, tags include frontend); position-mapping correctness across concurrent edits is load-bearing for every downstream patch. FULL per root §8.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Extends task 020's module against the well-specified ProseMirror `Mapping` primitive; default sonnet tier suffices. Effort raised to xhigh for position-mapping correctness (not a tier change).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>W2b</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Extends the interceptor from task 020 — same file/module; cannot run concurrently with 020.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>020</deps>
    <tags>frontend,docx</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2 days</estimated-effort>
    <assigned>unassigned</assigned>
    <started></started>
    <completed></completed>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Maintain an ordered, rebased operation log for each dirty editing session (design §5, "Capture" →
    "Maintain an ordered, rebased operation log per dirty session; ProseMirror position-mapping rebases as
    the user keeps editing"). As the user keeps editing, use ProseMirror `Mapping` (from `prosemirror-transform`,
    `notes/bridge-prior-art.md` §1) to rebase the positions of already-captured operations so the log stays
    internally consistent; on save, the client sends the ORDERED rebased log + the base version. This EXTENDS
    task 020's interceptor module (`widgets/stepOperationInterceptor.ts`) — it is not a new surface. An
    operation whose anchor falls inside content deleted by a later edit MUST be flagged (via `Mapping.mapResult`'s
    deleted signal), never silently dropped (mirrors `AnnotationReanchorService`'s "never silently drop"
    discipline). MIT ProseMirror base only — NO `@tiptap-pro/*` (NFR-03). This task maintains the log; it does
    NOT wire the actual save fetch (that is the Phase 5 save-path work) — but it produces the serialized log
    shape the save will send.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior React/TypeScript editor engineer fluent in ProseMirror position mapping (`Mapping`, `StepMap`,
    `mapResult`, bias, deleted-range detection). Understands D2 (anchors re-derive on apply) and I-7 (no
    text-search — rebasing is position-mapping, not content-match).
  </role>

  <goal>
    A per-session operation log that stays consistent as editing continues: after edit A then a later edit B
    that lands earlier in the same paragraph, A's anchor is rebased so it still resolves to A's intended
    position; the log serializes in document order together with a base version; an operation whose anchor
    falls inside content deleted by a later edit is flagged for review, not silently dropped. The serialized
    `{orderedOps, baseVersion}` shape is what the save path (Phase 5) will transmit.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §5 "Capture (frontend)": the op log is ordered + rebased per dirty session; ProseMirror
      position-mapping rebases as the user keeps editing; the client sends the ordered rebased log + base
      version on save. `notes/bridge-prior-art.md` §1 documents `Mapping.map(pos,bias)` / `mapResult` — which
      rebases any saved position forward through concurrent local edits and REPORTS if the position is inside
      deleted content. §4 is the "anchor survives concurrent edits" theory. This task extends the task-020
      interceptor (same module). "Base version" pairs with the server's version stamp (SPE eTag + projection
      schema version) that Phase 5 (task 050) asserts on save — this task just carries it in the log.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/stepOperationInterceptor.ts — EXTEND (task 020's module): add the ordered rebased op-log store + `Mapping`-based rebasing + `{orderedOps, baseVersion}` serialization</file>
      <file role="dependency-output">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/tasks/020-step-operation-interceptor.poml output — the per-transaction operations this log accumulates and rebases</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/AnnotationReanchorService.cs — the "never silently drop / surface for review" discipline to mirror for deleted-content ops</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/design.md §5 (Capture — rebased op log), §5.0</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/bridge-prior-art.md §1 (Mapping/mapResult), §4 (anchor drift)</file>
      <file role="spec">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/spec.md FR-03, FR-11, NFR-02, NFR-03</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="020" status="pending">Step→operation interceptor — produces the per-transaction operations this task accumulates, rebases, and orders. This task extends its module.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-03">The client MUST maintain an ordered, rebased operation log per dirty session and send the ordered rebased log + base version on save. Rebasing MUST use ProseMirror position-mapping, not re-diffing. Scope: the op-log store in the interceptor module.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / I-7, D2">Rebasing is POSITION-mapping (`Mapping`), never a text-search or content-match; anchors re-derive on apply. Scope: the rebase function.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / never silently drop">An operation whose anchor falls inside later-deleted content MUST be flagged (surfaced for review), NOT silently dropped — mirroring `AnnotationReanchorService`. Scope: the deleted-range handling in the rebase step.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec / NFR-03">MIT ProseMirror base only. MUST NOT add `@tiptap-pro/*`, AGPL, or commercial packages; no EigenPal runtime dependency. Scope: this task's imports.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">This task does not wire the save fetch; if the log's transmit is stubbed it MUST route through `@spaarke/auth` when Phase 5 wires it. Flagged so no ad-hoc token handling is introduced.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 / NFR-06">Rebasing correctness covered by colocated Vitest (full suite task 024). NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration, or ctor-null tests. Scope: tests under `src/`.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>ProseMirror Mapping/mapResult position rebasing; ordered op-log maintenance; base-version carry; never-silently-drop discipline; licensing</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/bridge-prior-art.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/design.md</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Mapping.mapResult" location="notes/bridge-prior-art.md §1">
        `Mapping.map(pos,bias)` / `mapResult` rebases a saved position forward through concurrent local edits and reports if it is inside deleted content — the exact primitive for keeping the op log consistent.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Never silently drop" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/AnnotationReanchorService.cs">
        AUTO/REVIEW/ORPHAN bands with an ambiguity guard that surfaces rather than drops — mirror this for ops whose anchor lands in deleted content.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the FULL rigor-level declaration (root §8). Load the knowledge files + `notes/bridge-prior-art.md` §1/§4. Confirm task 020 is complete (its module + per-transaction ops exist to accumulate). Note: this maintains the log; it does not wire the save fetch.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Op-log store">Extend `stepOperationInterceptor.ts` with an ordered per-session op-log store: append each captured operation in document order; retain a base version handle (SPE eTag + projection schema version, carried opaquely from load).</step>
    <step order="2" name="Rebase on continued editing">On each subsequent transaction, rebase the anchors of already-captured ops through the transaction's `Mapping` so the log stays consistent (an earlier same-paragraph edit shifts a later op's resolved position correctly).</step>
    <step order="3" name="Deleted-content flagging">When `mapResult` reports an op's anchor is inside deleted content, FLAG it (mark for review / surface), do NOT drop it. Checkpoint (context-handoff) per root §5 after this third step.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Serialize for save">Serialize the log as `{orderedOps, baseVersion}` in document order — the shape Phase 5's save transmits. Do NOT wire the actual fetch here.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Local tests + build">Add colocated Vitest tests: rebase-across-concurrent-edits (A then earlier B), document-order serialization, deleted-content flagging. Run `npm run build:prod` (NOT `npm run build`); confirm no `@tiptap-pro/*`.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Close-out">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set this task's status to ✅. Document any deviation in `projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <ui-tests>
    <ui-test name="Rebase keeps an earlier op consistent">
      <steps>In one paragraph, type text (edit A), then type more text at an earlier position in the same paragraph (edit B).</steps>
      <expected>A's logged anchor is rebased so it still resolves to A's intended location; the ordered log reflects both ops without corruption.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Log serializes in document order with a base version">
      <steps>Make edits in paragraphs 3, then 1, then 2; inspect the serialized log.</steps>
      <expected>Ops serialize in document order (para 1, 2, 3) with a single base version handle attached.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Op inside deleted content is flagged, not dropped">
      <steps>Type an insertion, then delete the surrounding range that contains that op's anchor.</steps>
      <expected>The affected op is flagged for review (surfaced), not silently removed from the log.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Dark-mode render (ADR-021)">
      <steps>Render the editor and any op-log / flagged-op affordance under the Fluent v9 dark theme provider.</steps>
      <expected>Any surfaced flag/affordance uses theme tokens and is legible in dark mode; rebasing behavior is theme-independent; no hard-coded light colors.</expected>
    </ui-test>
  </ui-tests>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If rebasing cannot disambiguate two operations that resolve to the same position after mapping (a genuine ordering ambiguity), STOP and surface it (root §6 / §6.5) rather than guessing an order — a wrong order silently corrupts the patch.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/stepOperationInterceptor.ts (extended: ordered rebased op-log + `{orderedOps, baseVersion}` serialization)</output>
    <output type="test">Colocated Vitest tests for rebasing/order/deleted-content flagging (extended in task 024)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">After edit A then a later edit B earlier in the same paragraph, A's anchor is rebased correctly and still resolves to its intended position.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The log serializes in document order with a single base version handle.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An op whose anchor falls inside later-deleted content is flagged, not silently dropped (negative case).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Rebasing uses ProseMirror `Mapping` position-mapping only — no text-search / content-match (I-7).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No `@tiptap-pro/*` / AGPL / EigenPal runtime dependency; `npm run build:prod` for the shared lib is green (NFR-03).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The dark-mode render (ADR-021) is legible with theme tokens.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Extends task 020's module (hence `parallel-safe:false`, same file). Maintains the log only — the actual
    save transmit is Phase 5 (task 050 version-stamp / re-anchor), which will send this `{orderedOps, baseVersion}`
    shape via `@spaarke/auth`. Client task (no BFF surface) — no publish-size / CVE gate.
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
